Z||000003||Voytek||08-22-2001||03:40 PM||||Sorry - I can't help you BUT, I sure would LOVE to see some pics of this!<BR>I was just thinking about this a couple of days ago when I was at a wrecking yard looking at an '87 STE with controls in the steering wheel.  That would definitely be neat in the Fiero!<P>Pics! Pics! Pics!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cozmo||08-22-2001||05:44 PM||||I let some friends borrow the Mavica for their vacation, they won't be back 'till Monday.  I am amazed how quickly I got used to a digital camera, they are REALLY handy!<BR>I'll get some pics up of the wheel and radio in the car then, maybe even lit up!<P>Hopefully by then I'll have solved the wire routing method through the column.  I'm going to the salvage yard and getting a Fiero column to tear apart and fit all the additional parts needed.<BR>I'm also going to grab the Bonneville climate control module (it looks difficult to get it to work, but it would be COOL) and a power amp for the rear speakers that is supposedly buried in the dash somewhere.<BR>I have searched everywhere and found NO schematics for this system.  I may have to get a factory manual (hope they're cheaper than Fiero ones... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).  If anybody has any info please share...<BR>I'm taking notes and will post them when they're more accurate.<P>BTW, we like people to vizit (esp. if they bring beer....).<P>BobC<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||08-22-2001||07:30 PM||||Hey Cozmo,<P>Be aware that the Fiero damper system for the A/C, heat, defroster is a electric motor driven system. Most other units use vacuum diaphragms that are controlled by the head unit. I don't know which the Bonne' system has but I didn't want to to waist a lot of time and $$$ pulling something that you can't use.<P>By the way, don't you have enough projects, yet?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||08-22-2001||08:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cozmo:<BR><B>...I may have to get a factory manual (hope they're cheaper than Fiero ones...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">).  If anybody has any info please share...<BR>I'm taking notes and will post them when they're more accurate.<P>BTW, we like people to vizit (esp. if they bring beer....).<P>BobC<BR>  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have a phone number for an organization (part of Delco electronics?) that will send you radio service literature at your request. Unfortunately, it's at work. <BR>The lady that answers the phone is not the most technical person, though. You will need to describe what kind of unit you have, and the year and model. You <I>might</I> actually get what you're looking for.<BR>The positive side of the situation is that the manuals are <I>free of charge</I>.<P>Barring any major disasters, I'll post the number tomorrow, from work. <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
